721 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Age being a command line encryption tool allows a user to encrypt arbitrary files for one or multiple parties\054 called recipients\056 Each recipient is then able to decrypt the file to get access to the original plain text\056 Each Age\055file has a header\054 storing data for the selected recipients\056 In Age\054 a 128 bit master key\054 called file key\054 is used\054 from which all further keys for authentication of the header and encryption of the plain text are derived\056 The user has no control over the file key used\054 instead it is selected randomly in the process of creating the Age\055file\056\n\nThe header of an Age\055file contains the encryption of the file key for the respective recipient\050s\051\056 Depending on which recipient type is used\054 from which there exist four in total\054 the key is encrypted in a different way\056 This process is called wrapping and the final wrapped file key\054 including a recipient type identifier\054 is called a recipient stanza\056\n\nFor derivation of the different keys\054 the key derivation function HKDF \13314\135is used\056 The derivation of the actual encryption key involves a randomly sampled nonce\054 which is placed inside an Age\055file directly after the header\054 such that the correct key can be derived in the decryption process\056\n\nThe final part of an Age\055file consists of the actual encryption of the pay\055load data\056 The Authenticated Encryption with Associated Data schemeChaCha20\055Poly1305 \13320\135 is used for this process\056)
     /K [ 112 ]
     /P 722 0 R
     /Pg 505 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

